# System states

- A list, table, account, or search has four states: loading, empty, error, success (data). Do not leave a blank white screen.
- Short content wait — spinner or local indicator. Page frame — skeleton, not a flashing empty layout.
- Operations longer than a few seconds — progress, not an endless spinner with no text.
- Empty: why it is empty and what to do (CTA). Distinguish “nothing yet” from “nothing found”.
- Error: what happened in plain language and Retry / back. Do not show a stack to the user.
- Success after an action: a lasting UI change or a short toast. Close the loop (button → loading → result).
- Mark busy: `aria-busy` on the region, status in a live region (`role="status"`), critical failure — `role="alert"`.
